I've never actually found one of these, but I've seen other players who did.

|> 7. Polymorph into a red dragon and lay an egg (#sit) and wait,

Did this once - I put on an unidentified uncursed ring, which happened to be
polymorph.  I poly'd into a rat and all my armor fell off, then turned into
an orange (I think) dragon.  I made sure to lay an egg before I changed
back to human!
This will work for any monster that lays eggs - according to the 3.0j
spoiler file, this includes all dragons (but not baby dragons), all nagas
(but not naga hatchlings), all spiders, all snakes, cockatrices, crocodiles,
all eels, all ants, long worms, puprle worms, and scorpions.

|> 8. polymorph into a black pudding and get attacked (try it!),

I've only done this in wizard mode.  It's no fun being a pudding though.

|> 9. polymorph into a were-anything and summon help (#monster).

I ALWAYS summon help once when I turn into a were-thing, so I can kill
whatever were-thing is attacking me.

|> 10. Possibly polymorph into a gremlin and find some water (haven't tried this).

I checked in wizard mode and found that if you polymorph into a gremlin,
you can use #monster to multiply in a fountain.
Your pet gremlins can also multiply, making more pet gremlins.

|> 11. Probably more ways. Oh yes, throw tripe/fresh edible corpses at a
|> chameleon when it's in the form of a cat or dog.

I did this once in a real game and thought it was incredibly funny!
Unfortunately, my pet suffered the fate of most chameleons - it turned
into some weak creature (I think a newt in this case) and got killed.

|> 12. I think someone wrote here that entering the astral plane with a
|> suitable high alignment gives you a guardian angel, but I'm still
|> playing 3.0j :(

I've checked this in wizard mode.

You forgot a few other ways:

13. Sometimes non-blessed magic lamps will give you a tame djinni who is
thankful for his release.  There is also a slight chance (I've heard 1/13)
that a smoky potion will contain a djinni, and he MIGHT give you a wish,
but also has a chance of being tame or hostile.

14. If you're an elf, invoke the Palantir of Westernesse (quest item).
(I haven't tested this - none of my elves have lived that long.)

15. When you're polymorphed into some minor demons (I forget which types)
sometimes you get some other tame demons ported in for you (just as these
same demons summon demons themselves).  There's even YAFM to go with this
one: "Some hell-p has arrived."
I know I've had this happen in a real game, and testing in wizard mode makes
it appear that you have to be in Gehennom for this to happen, while this
is not so when hostile devils summon help.  It also looks like you can't
summon major demons - It'd be too much of an advantage to have a tame Juiblex
following you around. 
I've produced this effect with bone devils and horned devils.

